\tag{fdip}
\title{Gaussian laws over symmetry sectors}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{The [real isotypic projectors](fdip-004V) split a field space,
and the [positive multiplicity matrices](fdip-0050) describe its
symmetry-preserving precisions. For a real Gaussian field this becomes
a product of independent sector laws, with real dimensions and
normalizers fixed by the scalar type. The result extends the
[two-sector product law](fdip-000M).}

\p{If the retained vertices form a union of group orbits, elimination
can be performed separately in each sector. Symmetry survives, but
the retained precision can change: keeping every other vertex of a
cycle produces a new cycle with different weight and mass. Its exact
periodic covariance explains the change of decay scale without
identifying a finite ring with an infinite lattice.}

